    "commit_message": "This PR adds **22 WOWII numbered-conjecture formalizations** from our\ninternal batches 3-9.\n\nPart **1 of 2** of splitting our internal batch `wowii-batches-3-9` (49\nfiles total after excluding one held back) into two reviewer-manageable\nPRs grouped semantically: this PR covers the `GraphConjecture<N>.lean`\nfiles indexed by individual WOWII conjecture numbers; the companion PR\n(#3821) covers the `Graph<InvariantName>.lean` files organized by graph\ninvariant topic.\n\n### Conjecture numbers in this PR\n7, 18, 31, 36, 59, 61, 65, 100, 101, 103, 109, 133, 142, 143, 144, 145,\n146, 160, 217, 291, 314, 315\n\n**Status distribution (per WOWII website):** T = 3, R = 1, F = 1, O =\n17.\n\n### Guarantees\n- Every file includes the **verbatim conjecture statement** from\nDeLaViña's WOWII page in the module docstring, along with the canonical\nsource URL. Reviewers can verify the formalization matches the source\nwithout navigating away from the diff.\n- Statements match the current authoritative website (re-audited against\nthe canonical source JSON we maintain in our private repo).\n\n### Notes\n- `GraphConjecture315.lean` already exists on `main`; this PR extends it\nwith the verbatim-statement docstring, additional definitions (total\ndominating sets, pendant vertices, well-totally-dominated), and the\nconjecture statement.\n- The file `GraphConjecture199.lean` is intentionally omitted here\nbecause an earlier version is already under review in #3796\n(`wowii-batch-2`). Additional test lemmas for Conjecture 199 will be\nsubmitted as a follow-up after #3796 merges.\n\n### Related\n- #3795 (batch 1, merged)\n- #3796 (batch 2, open)\n- Companion PR: #3821 (this batch, part 2/2 — named\n`Graph<InvariantName>` files)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Moritz Firsching <firsching@google.com>",
